---
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
export const prerender = true;

const updated = 'September 28, 2026';
const domain = 'freecrochetbags.com';
---

<TextPage title="Privacy Policy" eyebrow="Legal" description={`How ${SITE.name} collects, uses and protects your information.`}>
  <p><em>Last updated: {updated}</em></p>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} ("we", "us", "our") runs the website <strong>{domain}</strong>. We care about your privacy and try to
    collect as little information as possible. This policy explains what we collect, why, and the choices you have.
  </p>

  <h2>Information you give us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Newsletter:</strong> if you subscribe, we store your email address and the date you signed up. We use it
      only to send you occasional emails about new patterns.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact form:</strong> if you write to us, we store your name, email address and message so we can read
      and reply to it.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>You never need an account to browse or use our patterns.</p>

  <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting and security:</strong> our site is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any web server, Cloudflare processes
      standard technical data such as your IP address, browser type and the pages you request, in order to deliver the
      site and protect it from abuse.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fonts:</strong> our fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, so your browser connects to Google's servers, which
      receive your IP address.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Theme preference:</strong> if you switch to dark mode, your choice is saved in your own browser (local
      storage) so the site remembers it. This stays on your device and is never sent to us.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not use advertising cookies, tracking pixels or analytics tools that build a profile about you.</p>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To send the newsletter you asked for.</li>
    <li>To answer your messages.</li>
    <li>To keep the site running, secure and free of spam.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>We never sell, rent or trade your personal information.</strong> We only share it with the service providers
    that run the site (such as Cloudflare), and only as needed to provide the service, or when required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Newsletter emails are kept until you unsubscribe. Contact messages are kept only as long as needed to handle your
    request, then deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights and choices</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR in Europe or the CCPA in California), you may have the right
    to access, correct or delete your personal information, or to object to how we use it. You can unsubscribe from the
    newsletter or make any of these requests at any time through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, and we will
    respond as soon as possible.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served over an encrypted (HTTPS) connection and your information is stored with our hosting provider.
    No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure, but we take reasonable steps to protect your information.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is a general crafting site and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
    information from children. If you believe a child has sent us their information, please contact us and we will
    delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Our patterns may link to other websites. We are not responsible for their content or privacy practices, so please
    read their policies before sharing information with them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we will change the "Last updated" date at the top of this
    page. Please check back occasionally.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy? Send us a note through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. You can also read our
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>
</TextPage>
